@startuml
title Where each Pi clause goes: the lowering decision procedure, and the exit each of the seven clauses takes

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  DiamondBorderColor #1F2937
  DiamondFontColor #111827
}

start

:a clause of the ""equations"" or ""rewrites"" block;

if (every premise satisfies\n""premise_supported""?\n<i>only</i> ""Premise::Congruence"" is true\n(dovetail_report.rs:1456)) then (no)
  :**DECLARED, NOT LOWERED**\nrecorded in ""unsupported"";\nno e-graph rule, no native rule; <<#FEE2E2>>
  note right #FEE2E2
    **""ScopeExt""** exits here.
    Its premise is ""x # ...rest"" —
    a ""Premise::Freshness"", which
    returns ""false"" (:1464).
    Scope extrusion is instead
    realised as a NORMAL FORM by
    ""binder_congruence_nf"" — see
    figure ""pi-scope-extrusion"".
  end note
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (is it an equation?) then (yes)
  if (do both sides lower via\n""pattern_to_dovetail""?) then (no)
    :**DECLARED, NOT LOWERED**\n""lambda patterns require binder lowering""\n(dovetail_report.rs:1392); <<#FEE2E2>>
    note right #FEE2E2
      **""NewComm""** exits here.
      Both of its sides are
      ""(PNew ^x.(PNew ^y.P))"" —
      a ""PatternTerm::Lambda"", which
      the structural lowering
      declines. Binder permutation
      is instead realised by
      ""__bcn_close_new_run_canonical"".
    end note
    stop
  else (yes)
    :emit **TWO** ""dovetail::rules::RewriteRule""s,\n""::forward"" and ""::reverse""\n(lower_equation, :1488 / :1508); <<#DBEAFE>>
    note right #DBEAFE
      **""RepUnfold""** exits here.
      Verified in the generated output:
      ""Pi::equation::RepUnfold::forward""
      ""Pi::equation::RepUnfold::reverse""
    end note
    stop
  endif
else (no — a rewrite)
endif

if (""is_congruence_rule()""?) then (yes)
  :emit **NOTHING**\ncongruence closure is intrinsic\nto the e-graph (:1537); <<#EDE9FE>>
  note right #EDE9FE
    **""ParCong""** and **""NewCong""**
    exit here. They are still the
    normative statement of the
    reduction contexts; the engine
    simply satisfies them for free.
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (""is_comm_rewrite""?\n(dovetail_report.rs:609)) then (yes)
  :emit a typed ""NativeRule"" + a dispatch arm\non the **COMM lane** (typed_report.rs:1046); <<#DCFCE7>>
  note right #DCFCE7
    **""Comm""** (op 0) and
    **""CommAsync""** (op 1) exit here.
    Both are labelled
    ""Pi::rewrite::<name>"" in the
    generated rule set.
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

:the remaining classifiers —\n""is_substitution_rewrite"", ""is_structural_ac_rewrite"" —\nor the structural e-graph lowering; <<#EDE9FE>>
note right #EDE9FE
  No Pi clause reaches this exit.
  Each of the other lanes declines
  Pi's ""Comm"" by shape: the
  substitution lane requires the
  substitution to be the WHOLE RHS,
  and the structural-AC lane admits
  only reducts with NO substitution.
end note
stop

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBEAFE> blue | executable e-graph data (a bidirectional ""RewriteRule"") |
|<#DCFCE7> green | executable native data (a ""NativeRule"" plus its dispatch arm) |
|<#EDE9FE> violet | engine-supplied — nothing is emitted because nothing need be |
|<#FEE2E2> red | declared in the specification, NOT lowered onto this lane |
endlegend

@enduml
